# O2Suite, not O2PDPSuite: the point of this builder is that ubuntu2204 PR checks
# stop rebuilding the stack, and ubuntu2204/o2-alidist.env builds O2Suite. A
# release publishing a different top-level package would fill the store with
# things nobody asks for and leave the PR checks rebuilding anyway.
CI_NAME=build_O2Suite_daily_ubuntu2204
PACKAGE=O2Suite
PR_REPO=alisw/alidist
PR_BRANCH=master
ALIBUILD_DEFAULTS=o2
CHECK_NAME=release/O2Suite/daily-ubuntu2204
DONT_USE_COMMENTS=1

# The trigger is the O2PDPSuite daily tag even though we build O2Suite: alidist
# tags name a moment in the recipes, not an architecture or a package, so one tag
# legitimately drives both this and slc10-release. The _TEST variant is OPTIONAL
# as of 2026-09-01, so the ordinary daily cut is taken too -- that group was
# mandatory during bring-up, to keep an unproven builder away from real releases.
# Keep it in step with slc10-release/o2pdpsuite-daily.env: if the two regexes
# diverge, the builders silently run on different days.
TAG_REGEX='^O2PDPSuite-daily-%(date)-(?P<time>[0-9]{4})(?P<variant>_TEST)?$'

# NO test flags, unlike ubuntu2204/o2-alidist.env. A release is the artifact, not
# the test run: ALIBUILD_O2_TESTS adds -DENABLE_CASSERT=ON and runs the suites,
# which belongs to PR testing in O2 rather than to what we publish.
#
# Safe to differ, for a reason worth writing down. ALIBUILD_O2_TESTS is read by
# o2.sh but is NOT in the track_env of that recipe, so it changes the binary without
# changing the package hash -- normally a trap, because a consumer that sets it
# would silently reuse a build that ignored it. It does not bite here: the PR
# check lists "AliceO2Group/AliceO2 dev O2" in DEVEL_PKGS, and a development
# package folds devel_hash (commit_hash + local_hash) into its identity, so its
# O2 never matches a released O2 and is always rebuilt. What this builder
# actually supplies is everything BELOW O2 -- ROOT, GEANT4, boost, Clang -- none
# of which ALIBUILD_O2_TESTS touches.
#
# That reasoning stops holding the day a ubuntu2204 check builds O2 as a plain
# dependency rather than a devel package. If that changes, revisit this.
